There is an injective coefficient-preserving algebra map from $A_F$ into $$\bigl(\operatorname{Frac}(P_F)[X_*(T)]\bigr)^{\mathcal W},\qquad
 e^\lambda e^\gamma=e^{\lambda+\gamma}.$$ Besides $R$, the algebra is generated by the dressed classes associated with all nonzero positive and negative minuscule coweights. For $p\in P_F^{\mathcal W_\lambda}$, the class has expression $$\label{eq:minuscule}
 \sum_{\lambda'\in\mathcal W\lambda}
 e^{\lambda'}p_{\lambda'}
 \frac{\prod_{\beta\in\mathop{\mathrm{wt}}(N)}
           \beta^{(-\langle\beta,\lambda'\rangle)_+}}
      {\mathop{\mathrm{eu}}_T(T_{t^{\lambda'}}\mathop{\mathrm{Gr}}_G^\lambda)}.$$ Each distinct translate occurs once, and the dressing is translated with the coweight. Denote this class by $M_{\lambda,p}$. Weights $\beta$ include their flavor components, but pairings use only the gauge components; factors with exponent zero are omitted. The class has charge $[\lambda]$. On charge zero, the BFN grading is twice the ordinary polynomial degree of the rational coefficients in this description.

Let $u\in R$ be homogeneous of cohomological degree $d$, and suppose that in $A_F$ it has an expression $$\label{eq:neutral-word-relation}
 u=\sum_w M_{\lambda_{w,1},p_{w,1}}\cdots
                 M_{\lambda_{w,k_w},p_{w,k_w}},
 \qquad k_w\geq1,
 \qquad \sum_j[\lambda_{w,j}]=0\in\pi_1(G).$$ Every factor is a nontrivial dressed positive or negative minuscule generator of Proposition <a href="#prop:minuscule" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:minuscule">3</a>, and every word is homogeneous of degree $d$. Coefficients in $R$ may be included in the dressings. Choose an ordering of the factors of each word. There are $Z$ as above bounding their final lattices and a common truncation <a href="#eq:finite-lattice-space" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:finite-lattice-space">[eq:finite-lattice-space]</a> such that $$\label{eq:finite-relation-factorization}
 u\rho_Z=\sum_w\Psi_w
 \quad\text{in}\quad
 \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}^d_{\mathsf K,L}
       (\mathcal F_Z,\mathcal F_{\mathrm{pt}}).$$ Each $\Psi_w$ factors through a cohomological shift of $\mathcal F_{\mathop{\mathrm{Gr}}_G^{\lambda_{w,1}}}$. Only the endpoints are required to lie in $Z$ or in the neutral component; all intermediate lattices are included in the common truncation.

Assume $D\neq\varnothing$. The locus $\Sigma_Z$ is a closed graph $\Gamma\simeq U\times D$ in $M_Z$. There are compatible $\mathsf K$-equivariant identifications $$\label{eq:quadratic-vanishing-cycles}
 \Phi_{W_Z}\mathbb C_{M_Z}
 \simeq \iota_{\Gamma,*}\mathbb C_\Gamma[-2r],
 \qquad
 \Phi_{W_{\mathrm{pt}}}\mathbb C_{M_{\mathrm{pt}}}
 \simeq \iota_{D,*}\mathbb C_D[-2r].$$ Under these identifications, the test of $\rho_Z$ induces ordinary restriction $$\label{eq:quadratic-restriction}
 H_{\mathsf K}^*(U\times D)\longrightarrow H_{\mathsf K}^*(D)$$ with the same uniform shift on source and target. This map is split surjective and $R$-linear.

The quotient $B_0$ for the full topological torus satisfies the coefficientwise graded bound $$\label{eq:filtration-bound}
 \mathop{\mathrm{Hilb}}(B_0;q)\ \leq
 \sum_{m\in\mathcal M(\mathbf v)}
 q^{C(\mathbf v)-D_m+\mathbf w\cdot(\mathbf v-\mathbf l)}h_m(q).$$ Every exponent displayed in the sum is a nonnegative integer.

For every finite array $m$, $$\label{eq:cut-recurrence}
 \frac{1}{(q)_m}
 =\sum_{k+m'=m}
   q^{w(k)+b(k,m')}\frac{h_{m'}(q)}{(q)_k}.$$

In the formal power series ring $\mathbb C(q)[[z_i:i\in Q_0]]$, $$\label{eq:cut-generating-ratio}
 \sum_m z^{\|m\|}q^{-D_m-w(m)}h_m(q)
 =
 \frac{\displaystyle\sum_m
       z^{\|m\|}q^{-D_m-w(m)}/(q)_m}
      {\displaystyle\sum_m z^{\|m\|}q^{-D_m}/(q)_m}.$$

For a quiver with a loop at every vertex of positive dimension, $$\label{eq:hausel-cut-bound}
 P_{X_{\det}(v,w)}(q)
 =\sum_{\|m\|=v}
   q^{C(v)-D_m+w\cdot(v-l)}h_m(q).$$
